@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Equations)

Display and inline maths without backslashes, numbered equations, and equation libraries.

@section(Writing maths)

@subsection(@@eqn)

A display equation in IDoc math — no backslashes: frac{a}{b}, sqrt{x}, sin^2{alpha}, greek by name.

@eqn
frac{a}{b} = c
@end
@eqn(style=inline) x^2 @end

A numbered display with a wider gap to its number:
@eqn(gap=2em, label=gap1)
E = m c^2
@end

@subsection(@@eqi)

Inline math, short form of eqn(style=inline) — it flows with the prose.

@subsection(@@eqns)

Several lines of maths lined up at &, each line with its own number.

@eqns
f(x) &= (x+1)^2 @label(sq)
     &= x^2 + 2x + 1 @nonum
g(x) &= 3x
@end
as shown in @eqref(ohm)

@subsection(@@eqnnum)

A numbered display equation — referenceable with eqref.

@eqnnum(label=ohm)
V = I R
@end

@eqnnum(gap=3em)
F = m a
@end

@subsection(@@eqref)

Reference a numbered equation by its label.

@section(Equation libraries)

@subsection(@@dict)

Define a library of named equations, reusable with eq / eqsrc.

@dict(trig)
pythag: a^2 + b^2 = c^2
@end

@dict(geo)
Pythagorean: c^2 = a^2 + b^2
  label: Pythagorean theorem
  caption: c squared equals a squared plus b squared
  term: c | c | the hypotenuse
py = Pythagorean
@end

@subsection(@@eq)

Insert a library equation from a dict by name (read-only).

@eq(trig.pythag)

@eq(med.Beer-Lambert-Intensity, all)

@eq(fd.nv, num)
the value @eqi(x^2) grows

@dict(phys)
ohm: V = I R
  label: Ohm's law
  caption: voltage equals current times resistance
  expanded: the voltage across a resistor is the current through it times its resistance
  terms: V voltage; I current; R resistance
  source: Ohm, 1827
  author: A. Rivera
@end

Inline from the library: @eq(phys.ohm, inline).

@eq(phys.ohm, label)

@eq(phys.ohm, caption)

@eq(phys.ohm, expanded)

@eq(phys.ohm, terms)

@eq(phys.ohm, source)

@eq(phys.ohm, author)

@subsection(@@eqsrc)

Pull a library equation's SOURCE so you can edit it in place.

@eqsrc(trig.pythag)

@subsection(@@eqinfo)

A dictionary entry's stored fields as a block, without the equation: label, spoken caption, expanded caption, terms table, source, and who wrote and checked it.

@eqinfo(med.Beer-Lambert-Intensity)

@eqinfo(ee.Friis-Aperture, caption, terms)

@eqinfo(phys.ohm, label)

@eqinfo(phys.ohm, expanded)

@eqinfo(phys.ohm, source)

@eqinfo(phys.ohm, author)

@eqinfo(phys.ohm, all)
